                        <provenance type="#e" cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_199">Evesham,
                                Worcestershire. Benedictine abbey of St Mary the Virgin and St
                                Egwin</orgName><p>Gough Missals 33 was listed under Evesham abbey
                                (with a query) in the second edition of Medieval Libraries of Great
                                Britain (1964), with a footnote indicating that the book belonged to
                                the Chapel of the Battle Well. There were no relevant changes in the
                                Supplement (1987). The Evesham abbey attribution was not included in
                                MLGB3 (2010-2015). The corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great
                                Britain index card records the following information:</p><p>
                                <q>Orate pro bono statum magistri Johannis More decretorum doctoris
                                    qui hunc librum contulit capelle de le Batell welle</q> on the
                                verso of Te igitur leaf (fol. [C1]), pasted over. There is another
                                inscription on fol. [C4], similarly pased over. Liturgically
                                Evesham. For the Battle well see George May, <title>History of
                                    Evesham</title> (1845). I find no mention of the
                            chapel.</p></provenance>
                        <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_1014">South
                                Littleton, Worcestershire. Parish church</orgName>
                            <p>This attribution was rejected in the second edition of Medieval
                                Libraries of Great Britain (1964), which did not change in the
                                Supplement (1987). The corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great
                                Britain index card records the following information, which was
                                deemed unsatisfactory for an attribution:</p>
                            <p>
                                <q>Missale sarum ecclesiae de South Littleton</q> (flyeaf i, s.
                                xvii?). Early s. xvi documents at end and annotations to text show
                                that it belonged early to South Littleton Church (compare
                                    <title>Summary Catalogue</title> after 18345). Fol. 184v margin:
                                    <q>De sancto Kanuto rege et martire require ...</q>. After 185
                                are two leaves containing the form <q>In translacione sancti Egwini
                                    officium</q>. Fols. 237v, 238 margin is <q>Missa de reliquis
                                    officium sapienciam ... pro sanctorum tuorum egwini wistani
                                    Oswaldi Odulfi atque Credani merita gloriosa et aliorum
                                    sanctorum quorum reliquiarum in presenti requiescent ecclesia
                                    ...</q></p></provenance>
                    </history>
